      "principle": "The term 'cruelty' consists of unwarranted and unjustifiable conduct causing suffering and distress, thereby destroying peace of mind.",
      "held": "As ground for divorce the term 'cruelty' consists of unwarranted and unjustifiable conduct on part of defendant causing other spouse to endure suffering and distress, thereby destroying peace of mind and making living with such spouse unbearable.",
