      "principle": "Mental cruelty must be of such a nature that the parties cannot reasonably be expected to live together.",
      "held": "Mental cruelty in Section 13(1)(ia) can broadly be defined as that conduct which inflicts upon the other party such mental pain and suffering as would make it not possible for that party to live with the other.",
